Find the average cost function represented by {eq}\frac {C}{x}{/eq}. Recall that a rational function is any function that can be expressed in the form {eq}\frac {f(x)}{g(x)}{/eq}, where {eq}f(x){/eq} and {eq}g(x){/eq} are both polynomials. To find the average cost function, we need to divide the total cost by the number of bears produced:

$$\begin{align}

\frac{C}{x} &= \frac{12x + 1600}{x}

\\ &= \frac{x(12) + 1600}{x}

\\ &= \frac{x(12)}{x} + \frac{1600}{x}

\\ &= 12 + \frac{1600}{x}

\end{align}

